  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14227574/assets/6f38e64442bb383f218dede5a88740653f958864d3284ce09c3e1bb99ed7e421.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above shows the relationship between the time (in hours) some college students spend studying the night before an exam and the time they spend sleeping that night. Assuming this trend continues, estimate the time a student spends studying if that student gets only $3.75$ hours of sleep.\n\n*Hint: Assume the trend is linear and that the trend line passes through the points $(2,7.5)$ and $(4,5).$*",
